<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Firuz Shah Bahmani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1397">1397</a>–<a href="/years/1422">1422</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Taj ud-Din Firuz Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taj ud-Din Firuz Shah was sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> from 1397 to 1422. A learned ruler, he encouraged Persian scholars and built the palace city of Firuzabad on the Bhima river. He fought several wars against Vijayanagara, but in 1420 suffered a heavy defeat at Pangal, and in 1422 he gave up the throne to his brother Ahmad Shah shortly before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/firuz-shah-bahmani.jpg" alt="Firuz Shah Bahmani" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Smloverboy4 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haft_Gumbad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Firuz Shah</b> (r. 1397–1422) won several campaigns, but in 1420 he suffered a heavy defeat at Pangal.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate · Military</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalaburagi">Kalaburagi</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=17.33,76.83&amp;year=1409" aria-label="Kalaburagi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6638 1520 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Firuz Shah Bahmani"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7088 1790h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7088 1790h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=17.33,76.83&amp;year=1409">What was here in 1409? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
